WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.640
- [Instructor] So as
some of you already know,

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.120
I really enjoy eating a good avocado,

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.480
which, despite its appearance

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.010
that it looks like a vegetable,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.930
but it's actually a fruit.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.000
And let's say that I eat
two avocados per day,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.800
and I eat two avocados
per day for six days.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.840
Now, there's a couple of
ways that I could think

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.060
about how many avocados did I eat?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.450
I could say, hey, I eat two a day,

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.550
and I'm going to do that for six days,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.940
so I'm gonna add six twos together.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.940
So it'll be two, plus two,
plus two, plus two, plus two,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.590
plus two, I have six
twos right over there.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.930
And then I can add them together.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.800
And we could say two plus two is four.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.290
You add another two, you get to six.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.520
You add another two, you get to eight.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.980
Yet another two to get to 10.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.690
Yet another two, you get to 12.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.970
And that all is fine,
but there's an easier way

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.490
to express this repeated addition.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:00.570
One way is to view it as multiplication.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.360
Instead of just writing out six twos

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.560
and adding them together,
mathematicians have come up

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.780
with a neater way of writing that.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.490
Let's say, okay, we're going
to add up a bunch of twos.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.490
How many twos are we going to add up?

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.540
We're going to have six of those twos,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.950
and we need to come up with
some type of a symbol for it.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.940
So we will use this X-looking thing.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.100
And so, six times two can be viewed

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.770
as repeated addition in
exactly this same way.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.150
So six times two would be equal to 12.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.960
And we could go the other way around.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.960
If someone were to ask you,
what is four times three?

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.600
Pause this video and see
if you can write it out

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.790
as repeated addition, like we saw up here.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.890
Well, one way to interpret this is to say,

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.660
this is four threes, so
we could say this is equal

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:56.530
to three, plus three,
plus three, plus three.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.520
And three plus three is
six, six plus three is nine,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.280
nine plus three is equal to 12.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.770
You might be familiar with skip counting,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.240
and you would say three, six, nine, 12.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.710
Just out of curiosity,

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.380
what do you think three
times four is going to be?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.800
Pause this video and try to represent it

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.753
as repeated addition, and then
see what you come up with.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.470
Well, we can interpret
this as three fours.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.160
And so, we could say this is going

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.520
to be four, plus four, plus four.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.669
And if we skip count fours,
we'd have four, eight, 12,

00:02:32.669 --> 00:02:35.570
(chuckles) I was about to
go to 16, four, eight, 12.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.440
So this is going to be 12.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.140
So this is interesting,
at least for this example,

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.690
for these two examples,
I got to the same thing.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.620
Four times three got me the same result

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.390
as three times four, interesting.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.470
I wonder if that's always true.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.780
But anyway, big picture from this video is

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.780
that you can view multiplication
as repeated addition.

